# Turns the analysis into the paths the robot puts on the board.
#
# A service rather than an action: it is one pass of plain geometry, a couple of
# milliseconds, with nothing to report on the way and nothing worth cancelling.
#
# All three paths come from one call because they share a layout - where the
# eraser sweeps is decided by where the fixed labels end. Asking for them
# separately would let a parameter change slide one past the other, and the way
# that shows up is the robot wiping text that was meant to stay.
tvarometr_interfaces/FaceAttributes attributes
---
bool success
string message

# Positions in metres, in the board's own frame: z=0 is on the board, z>0 is
# lifted. Each path starts and ends lifted.

# The fixed column of labels. Drawn once, onto a clean board.
geometry_msgs/PoseArray labels
# This run's answers, in the right-hand column. Drawn every cycle.
geometry_msgs/PoseArray values
# Overlapping sweeps across the value column, clear of the labels. Covers the
# whole column whatever the last values were, so it does not depend on them.
geometry_msgs/PoseArray erase
